<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<odoo>
    <data noupdate="1">
        <!--
            When this shop started billing locker drop-offs through Odoo.
            Anything that reached the lockers before it was settled some other
            way, and is treated as sold the moment it syncs in - see
            laundry.locker.billing.override.

            Seeded so that a database installing this module for the first
            time does not pull in years of long-collected bags and hand the
            counter a queue of them. Once it exists it belongs to the
            database: change it in Settings > Technical > System Parameters,
            not here.

            Written through a method rather than as a <record> on
            ir.config_parameter, because a record INSERTs and the key is
            unique - installing into a database where the cutoff had already
            been set by hand aborted the install on a duplicate key. The
            method declines to touch a cutoff that is already set, so it is
            safe whether or not the parameter is there, and safe to run
            twice.

            Individual refs on either side of this line - one sold later
            outside Odoo, one still genuinely waiting despite being older -
            are exceptions, and go under Lockers > Billing Overrides.

            SHOP TIME, not UTC: this is compared against the New Laundry
            column, and that column is read off the screen in shop time.
            Everything from 4am on Sep 26 2026 is still the counter's work.

            4am rather than midnight because the small hours of the 26th
            were still being settled the old way - the line falls where the
            shop's practice changed, not where the date does. The time is
            written out in full: this decides a thousand rows, and it should
            not need anyone to know which end of the day it falls on.
        -->
        <function model="laundry.locker.billing.override"
                  name="_laundry_seed_billed_before"
                  eval="('2026-09-26 04:00:00',)"/>
    </data>
</odoo>
